rue" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Example_Event_Spreads"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Outcomes"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Success_Calculation"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gating_Conditions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Selection_Process"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Event_Categories"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Events"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Daily_Cycle"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Operations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Elara.27s_Passive_Roles"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Elara's_Passive_Roles"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Available_Actions_in_the_Office"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Elara.27s_Office_.E2.80.94_The_Management_Hub"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Elara's_Office_—_The_Management_Hub"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Brothel_Decor_Level"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Brothel_Promotion_Level"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Reputation_.2820.2B_levels.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Reputation_(20+_levels)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Brothel_Systems"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Strategic_Notes"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Report_Integration"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Taming_Session_Actions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Work_Mechanics_.28Tamed_.E2.89.A5_30.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Work_Mechanics_(Tamed_≥_30)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Tamed_Meter_.E2.80.94_The_Core_Mechanic"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Tamed_Meter_—_The_Core_Mechanic"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Raven.27s_Sessions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Raven's_Sessions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Exit"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Training"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Praise"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Talk"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Session_Menu"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Availability_Rules_.26_Visit_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Availability_Rules_&amp;_Visit_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Daily_Upkeep"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Full_Skill_Library"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_Skills_Work"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Skills_System"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Stress.2FHealth_at_a_Glance"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Stress/Health_at_a_Glance"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="High-Loyalty_Bonus"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Refuse-to-Work_.28Low_Loyalty_Strike.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Refuse-to-Work_(Low_Loyalty_Strike)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Sick_Rest_.28Health.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Sick_Rest_(Health)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Exhausted_Rest_.28Stress.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Exhausted_Rest_(Stress)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Stat_Strategy_Summary"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Fame_.28not_directly_trainable.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Fame_(not_directly_trainable)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Charisma"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Appearance"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Ability"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Dexterity"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Intelligence"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Stamina"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_Each_Primary_Stat_Actually_Does"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gastoff.27s_Commissions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gastoff's_Commissions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Courtyard_Outside_Hub"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_West_Hallway_Hub"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Entering_the_Brothel"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Navigating_the_Rose_.26_Thorn"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Navigating_the_Rose_&amp;_Thorn"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Hotel_Operation_Mode_.28Alternative.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Hotel_Operation_Mode_(Alternative)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Overview"></span>
<h2>Start running the Rose &amp; Thorn</h2>
<p>The <strong>Rose &amp; Thorn</strong> is your business in <strong>Medieval → Kings Demesne</strong>. To gain ownership, follow the King’s early supply problem through Wilfred’s delivery, then return to the Throne Room between <strong>10:00 and 16:59</strong> for <strong>The Royal Appointment</strong>. Ownership opens Elara’s Office and the Master Bedroom and recruits Elara; it does not require buying the building for cash.</p><p>Enter Elara’s Office for <strong>Establishing Operations</strong> and choose <strong>Brothel</strong> or <strong>Hotel</strong>. This is a one-time business choice. The core staffing, bedrooms, income, cleaning and reputation systems are shared, while daily event pools, presentation and some checks differ. Hotel mode also does not offer Receive a Client. This guide uses the business’s name when the same instruction applies to both modes.</p><ol><li>Go to <strong>Worker Quarters → Manage Workers</strong> to check Stress, Health, Loyalty, equipment and spendable worker EXP.</li><li>Open <strong>Manage Rooms</strong> for bedrooms, apprentice assignments and, later, vacations.</li><li>Advance an in-game day, then choose <strong>Get Business Report</strong> in Elara’s Office. Read the completed day and collect pending earnings.</li><li>Keep cleaning capacity ahead of new clients. Recruit maids, use sensible assignments, and manually clean if necessary.</li></ol><p>This page covers access and daily decisions. Exact pay, reputation, cleaning and tax formulas are on <a href="game-systems-brothel-stats-and-calculations.html">Brothel Stats and Calculations</a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-daily-checks">
<h2>A short daily management routine</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Working</th><td data-label="What it means">Ordinary clients, pay, work EXP, stress, Fame roll and mess</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Resting / Sick</th><td data-label="What it means">Does not work; the day rest finishes also earns no ordinary pay</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Refused work</th><td data-label="What it means">Possible below 30 Loyalty; worker-specific chance</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ballroom trainee</th><td data-label="What it means">Replaces client work with training EXP; +10% business reputation, 15% normal-net fee</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">On vacation</th><td data-label="What it means">No ordinary work; daily recovery and Loyalty buffer up to 150</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Stress above <strong>75 after work</strong> starts two rest days. If that did not trigger first, zero Health starts four sick days, or three with Willow active. Rest completion restores full Health and clears Stress, but work resumes on a later report. Loyalty below 30 can cause refusal; above 80 can trigger a personal bonus. Exactly 30 and exactly 80 do not cross those thresholds.</p><p>Check those states before assuming a room or income bonus failed. Working hours govern ordinary visits and private bookings; the business’s daily calculation does not run an hourly client simulation. Keep report collection regular: missing completed days use the current roster and assignments when calculated, rather than a historical snapshot.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-navigation">
<h2>Find the right room</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Hub</th><th scope="col">Useful paths and controls</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Entrance</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Elara’s Office, Master Bedroom, Worker Quarters, West Hallway; unlocked service rooms</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">West Hallway</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Arcane Room, Kitchen, Courtyard, Training Room and other unlocked rooms; Clean Establishment</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Courtyard</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Pool, Menagerie and Garden routes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Upper Floor</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">VIP Lounge, Vespa’s Room and the specialist rooms reached from here</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Nurse’s Room</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Cellar access when the personal route allows it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Brothel Dungeon</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Cell Corridor after construction</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Worker Quarters</th><td data-label="Useful paths and controls">Management, visits, Ryia’s Room after recruitment</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A named room you can walk into and an apprentice tile in Manage Rooms are related but different controls. Recruitment and personal progress open many doors. The Upper Floor opens with Vixen or Vespa. The Garden is reachable with Audrey or A.R.I.A.; Foxy’s and Ryia’s rooms open through their own recruitment, while Cinnamon’s room requires her completed performance-room recruitment. If a door is absent, consult that character’s current Objectives rather than buying unrelated bedroom upgrades.</p><p>The Secret Room is special access through Azariel’s redeem-code content; its door’s <strong>Investigate Strange Door</strong> action opens the code entry. General business growth does not unlock that room automatically.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-workers"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Three-Girl_Worker_Bonding"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Selection_Methods"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Non-Worker_Residents"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Visitable_Workers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers_Interactions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Manage_Workers_Screen"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_Skills_by_Worker_.2830_Recruitable_Workers.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Starting_Skills_by_Worker_(30_Recruitable_Workers)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Status_.E2.80.94_Rest.2C_Sickness.2C_and_Strikes"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Status_—_Rest,_Sickness,_and_Strikes"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Loyalty"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Data_Structure"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Workers"></span>
<h2>The 30 workers and their passives</h2>
<p>Recruitment is personal progression, not a shared hiring-price menu. Ava &amp; Eva occupy one worker slot. The table gives route pointers and ordinary shift windows; the ending hour is exclusive and overnight shifts continue past midnight. Raven uses her own sessions rather than the ordinary visit selector.</p><details><summary>Open the roster, shifts and recruitment pointers</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Worker</th><th scope="col">Ordinary shift</th><th scope="col">Innate passive</th><th scope="col">Where to progress</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-elara.html">Elara</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">10:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Assistant</td><td data-label="Where to progress">The Royal Appointment</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-sophie.html">Sophie</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">12:00–20:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Loyal Heart</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Rescue in the Grand Bazaar back alley</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-honey.html">Honey</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Organizer</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Rural Farm personal route</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-sandra.html">Sandra</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">16:00–24:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Master Performer</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Bards Guild personal route</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-grace.html">Grace</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">14:00–22:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Meditation</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Grace and Sashina’s personal objectives; business rank 5+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-cinnamon.html">Cinnamon</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">15:00–23:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Acrobatics</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Complete her personal route and build her performance room; Menagerie needed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-raven.html">Raven</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">18:00–02:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Dungeon Master</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 20 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-shadow.html">Shadow</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">20:00–04:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Pickpocket</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Thieves Guild personal arrangement; faction reputation 120+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-foxy.html">Foxy</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">19:00–03:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Fast Learner</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Forest Clearing personal route</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-bellavia.html">Bellavia</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">21:00–04:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Sucking</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Follow current personal Objectives</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-valkyra.html">Valkyra</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">13:00–21:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Bodyguard</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 30 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-lindia.html">Lindia</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">12:00–20:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Perfect Memory</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 7 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-ava-and-eva.html">Ava &amp; Eva</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">12:00–24:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Natural Beauty</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Entrance arrival with Vixen recruited and business rank 14+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-gem.html">Gem</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">14:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Mining</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Complete Gem’s and Lyra’s linked objectives and Worker Quarters contract</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-jade.html">Jade</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">08:00–16:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Accountant</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon trade or the separate back-alley opportunity</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-pixie.html">Pixie</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">07:00–23:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Fast Learner</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Complete her dungeon encounter route and later reunion</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-brandy.html">Brandy</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">18:00–02:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Crowd Pleaser</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Her recruitment H 2 H; business rank 8+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-willow.html">Willow</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">18:00–23:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Healer</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Back-alley introduction and healing-partnership route</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-vixen.html">Vixen</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">11:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Charming Personality</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Personal partnership; business rank 10+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-kasumi.html">Kasumi</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">14:00–20:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Oracle</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Personal route, starting at business rank 6 and continuing through 10</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A.R.I.A.</th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">20:00–04:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Adaptive Learning</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 45 progression</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-vespa.html">Vespa</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">19:00–01:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Queen</td><td data-label="Where to progress">King’s Court objective chain, concluding at business rank 18+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-audrey.html">Audrey</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">08:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Gardener</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 35 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-whiskers.html">Whiskers</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">20:00–04:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Focused</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 5 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-ember.html">Ember</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">21:00–03:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Resilient</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon Floor 50 encounter</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-momosagi.html">Momosagi</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">08:00–22:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Insatiable</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Dungeon personal scenario; player Taming 20+</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-sashimi.html">Sashimi</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">15:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Siren Song</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Pool personal route; Her Own Current</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-maize.html">Maize</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">09:00–17:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Heartbreaker</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Fighters Guild bounty encounter from Floor 35</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-pepper.html">Pepper</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">00:00–24:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Bunny Hop</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Easter reward and introduction</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="character-ryia.html">Ryia</a></th><td data-label="Ordinary shift">10:00–18:00</td><td data-label="Innate passive">Perfect Memory</td><td data-label="Where to progress">Peasant Huts personal route and recruitment</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p>Innate work effects are small and specific: income passives add 5% personal pay; Fast Learner, Perfect Memory, Mining and Adaptive Learning add 1 work EXP; stress passives prevent 1 work stress; Master Performer, Acrobatics, Focused and Siren Song add 3 percentage points to double pay; Organizer/Gardener add 2 cleaning; Insatiable adds 1 client; Oracle/Queen add 1 daily reputation. The six service-role passives explain their room benefits, without adding a duplicate bonus. The <a href="game-systems-brothel-stats-and-calculations.html#en-passives">calculation reference</a> gives the exact order.</p><p>Poppy, Blinky, Sherry, Azariel, Esperanza and Muramasa are service hosts or residents, not extra ordinary worker entries. The six maids and captured monsters also use separate management systems.</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot" style="max-width: 1085px"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Worker management separates Health, Loyalty, Stress, EXP, attributes and innate passives. These two early workers show example values." href="../assets/images/wiki/brothel-guide/en-worker-management-full.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Worker management separates Health, Loyalty, Stress, EXP, attributes and innate passives. These two early workers show example values." decoding="async" height="215" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/brothel-guide/en-worker-management.webp" width="1085"/></a><figcaption>Worker management separates Health, Loyalty, Stress, EXP, attributes and innate passives. These two early workers show example values.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-bedrooms"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Worker_Bedroom_Intimate_Plots"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Room_Service_.E2.80.94_Poppy.27s_Signature_Offering"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Room_Service_—_Poppy's_Signature_Offering"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Kitchen_.26_Room_Service"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Kitchen_&amp;_Room_Service"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Service_Room_Apprenticeship_Effects"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_to_unlock_the_Specialty_Rooms"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Specialty_Rooms"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Upgrading_workers.27_rooms_and_their_effects"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Upgrading_workers'_rooms_and_their_effects"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Room_Management_Screen"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers_Rooms_.26_Upgrades"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers_Rooms_&amp;_Upgrades"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers.27_Room"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers'_Room"></span>
<h2>Buy worker-bedroom upgrades</h2>
<p>In <strong>Worker Quarters → Manage Rooms</strong>, use the upgrade button on the worker’s bedroom tile. Bedrooms start at 1 and cap at 5. Each row is the additional cost to reach that level. <strong>C/R/E = Common/Rare/Epic</strong>; Materials, Fabrics and Ingredients are separate resource payments. Bedroom purchases do not advance time.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Target level</th><th scope="col">Gold</th><th scope="col">Materials</th><th scope="col">Fabrics</th><th scope="col">Ingredients</th><th scope="col">Pay maximum / daily reputation / clients</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="Gold">$1, 000</td><td data-label="Materials">20 C+5 R</td><td data-label="Fabrics">10 C</td><td data-label="Ingredients">5 C</td><td data-label="Pay maximum / daily reputation / clients">×1.10 / +1 / +0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="Gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="Materials">40 C+10 R</td><td data-label="Fabrics">20 C+5 R</td><td data-label="Ingredients">15 C+3 R</td><td data-label="Pay maximum / daily reputation / clients">×1.25 / +3 / +1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td data-label="Gold">$25, 000</td><td data-label="Materials">25 R+5 E</td><td data-label="Fabrics">15 R+3 E</td><td data-label="Ingredients">10 R+2 E</td><td data-label="Pay maximum / daily reputation / clients">×1.40 / +5 / +2</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td data-label="Gold">$100, 000</td><td data-label="Materials">15 E</td><td data-label="Fabrics">10 E</td><td data-label="Ingredients">8 E</td><td data-label="Pay maximum / daily reputation / clients">×1.60 / +7 / +3</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>These are the bonuses for the room’s current level, not bonuses to add together from every row. Reputation is a flat daily contribution, not permanent Fame. At level 5, all 30 bedrooms could contribute 210 daily reputation before business modifiers; only employees who actually work contribute their row’s daily reputation. Added clients also increase mess and usually work stress.</p><p>Specialty-room staffing is different: its effective level usually means unlocked base plus assigned apprentices. Do not look for the old paid specialty-room upgrade ladder. Upkeep includes $20 per counted room level, including all defined worker bedrooms; see the <a href="game-systems-brothel-stats-and-calculations.html#en-building-income">upkeep formula</a> before expanding everything at once.</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Paid employee-bedroom levels and service-room apprentice assignments use separate controls. Example rooms and resources." href="../assets/images/wiki/brothel-guide/en-room-management.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Paid employee-bedroom levels and service-room apprentice assignments use separate controls. Example rooms and resources." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/brothel-guide/en-room-management.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>Paid employee-bedroom levels and service-room apprentice assignments use separate controls. Example rooms and resources.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-apprentices"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Apprenticeship_Strategy_2"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Elara_as_an_Apprentice_Master"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Apprenticeship_Strategy"></span>
<h2>Assign apprentices and service rooms</h2>
<p>Click a specialty tile in <strong>Manage Rooms</strong>, choose an available employee, and use <strong>Remove</strong> to free a slot. Most rooms allow <strong>three apprentices</strong>; the Ballroom allows <strong>one trainee</strong>. The worker must be active, unassigned elsewhere and not vacationing. Worker room masters—Elara, Raven, Valkyra, Willow and Vixen—cannot be apprentices. Ordinary apprentices still earn client income unless the room explicitly replaces work.</p><details><summary>Room access, effects and tradeoffs</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Room</th><th scope="col">Access</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Master Bedroom</th><td data-label="Access">Starting room</td><td data-label="Effect">Assigned workers: +50% work EXP, no positive daily work/event stress</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Elara’s Office</th><td data-label="Access">Starting room</td><td data-label="Effect">+5% business income and reputation per apprentice</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Maids Quarters</th><td data-label="Access">Acquire a maid</td><td data-label="Effect">+10 team cleaning per apprentice</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Infirmary</th><td data-label="Access">Recruit Willow</td><td data-label="Effect">Willow active: base work stress 7, sickness 3 days; apprentices prevent incoming work stress</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Security</th><td data-label="Access">Recruit Valkyra</td><td data-label="Effect">Daily event chance +8 pp, +5 pp per apprentice, final chance capped 95%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Brothel Dungeon</th><td data-label="Access">Recruit Raven</td><td data-label="Effect">Assigned apprentices cannot gain Stress or lose Loyalty; training stress 0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bar</th><td data-label="Access">Recruit Brandy; rank 8+ route</td><td data-label="Effect">+5% business income/reputation and 10 mess; each apprentice +1%, +1 mess and +2 personal clients</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kitchen</th><td data-label="Access">Poppy’s arrival at rank 4+</td><td data-label="Effect">Each apprentice: one randomly distributed daily client; improves Room Service</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Arcane Room</th><td data-label="Access">Blinky’s arrival at rank 7+</td><td data-label="Effect">+1 effective Decor per apprentice</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Secret Room</th><td data-label="Access">Azariel’s special access</td><td data-label="Effect">+1 work EXP per apprentice for every working employee</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Menagerie</th><td data-label="Access">Gastoff commission; rank 9+</td><td data-label="Effect">+1 effective Promotion per apprentice</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">VIP Lounge</th><td data-label="Access">Recruit Vixen; rank 10+ route</td><td data-label="Effect">Vixen and apprentices: +1 client, ×2 personal pay, ×2 mess</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Esperanza’s Ballroom</th><td data-label="Access">The Art of Nobility; rank 7+, Esperanza Friend, Elara Known</td><td data-label="Effect">One trainee: replacement EXP, +10% reputation, 15% normal-net fee</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Training Room</th><td data-label="Access">Build room, then Muramasa’s A Wider Ring</td><td data-label="Effect">0/1–2/3 apprentices: player-stat gains 2–5/2–6/3–7; 2+ apprentices reduce time to 100 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p>Early Office staffing improves both income and reputation. Infirmary staffing is more valuable as the roster grows; Medicine improves prevention further. Master Bedroom protects against <em>daily</em> stress, while the Dungeon also protects training stress and Loyalty. VIP doubles mess, and a Ballroom trainee gives up ordinary earnings and charges a fee. Assignments can also raise upkeep, so choose for the problem you actually have.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-clothing"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Two_Ways_to_Upgrade_Clothing"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Clothing_Levels_.281.E2.80.936.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Clothing_Levels_(1–6)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers_Clothing_.26_Items"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Workers_Clothing_&amp;_Items"></span>
<h2>Clothing levels and Fernando’s fittings</h2>
<p>Workers start at clothing 1 and cap at 6. Clothing improves the daily pay range and adds 0/1/2/3/4/5 flat daily reputation at levels 1–6. The last level is a separate <strong>MAX Worker Clothing</strong> action at Fernando’s Tailor Shop, not the ordinary fitting.</p><p>Fernando’s <strong>Worker Clothing</strong> and <strong>MAX Worker Clothing</strong> share <strong>one fitting per day</strong>, available <strong>06:00–20:59</strong>, taking <strong>30 minutes</strong>. He randomly chooses an eligible active worker. Below level 5, each worker can receive at most <strong>two ordinary Fernando upgrades</strong>. A worker at level 5 can receive the final MAX fitting, even after those earlier fittings.</p><p>The ordinary global price ladder starts at <strong>$300 and 10/5/1 Common/Rare/Epic Fabrics</strong>, rising with every completed fitting and stopping at tier 50: <strong>$500, 000 and 250/150/99 Fabrics</strong>. MAX costs <strong>double the current tier</strong>, with minimums of <strong>$5, 000 and 100/50/25 Fabrics</strong>. MAX also advances that shared price counter. You cannot choose which eligible worker receives the random fitting.</p><p>The separate <strong>A Guest’s Thanks</strong> follow-up can raise an eligible working employee’s clothing for free, only through level 5. Check the Entrance after a report announces a grateful guest. It does not spend Fernando’s fitting or advance his cost ladder. The opportunity uses Charisma+Appearance in Brothel mode and Charisma+Intelligence in Hotel mode; it does not require the NTS booking setting.</p><details><summary>All 50 fitting tiers and MAX quotes</summary><p>The fabric columns are Common/Rare/Epic. The displayed next quote follows your total number of fittings, not that employee’s clothing level.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Tier</th><th scope="col">Ordinary gold</th><th scope="col">Ordinary fabrics</th><th scope="col">MAX gold</th><th scope="col">MAX fabrics</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$300</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">10/5/1</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$350</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">15/7/2</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$400</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">25/10/3</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$500</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">32/13/4</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$550</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">40/16/5</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$600</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">46/20/6</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">100/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$700</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">52/24/7</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">104/50/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$900</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">58/27/8</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">116/54/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$1, 000</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">64/31/9</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">128/62/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$1, 200</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">70/35/10</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">140/70/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">11</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$1, 400</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">76/39/12</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">152/78/25</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">12</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$1, 600</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">82/43/14</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">164/86/28</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">13</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$1, 800</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">88/47/16</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">176/94/32</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">14</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$2, 100</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">94/51/18</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">188/102/36</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">15</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$2, 500</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">100/55/20</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 000</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">200/110/40</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">16</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$2, 900</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">106/59/23</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$5, 800</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">212/118/46</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">17</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$3, 400</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">112/63/26</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$6, 800</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">224/126/52</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">18</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$3, 900</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">118/67/29</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$7, 800</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">236/134/58</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">19</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$4, 600</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">124/71/32</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$9, 200</td><td data-label="MAX fabrics">248/142/64</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">20</th><td data-label="Ordinary gold">$5, 300</td><td data-label="Ordinary fabrics">130/75/35</td><td data-label="MAX gold">$10, 600</td><td data